---
import Todo from '@/components/ui/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import IndustryLayout from '@/layouts/IndustryLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How small a wire can you coil?',
    a: 'Down to 0.40 mm. That is the bottom of our standard range. Below that, ask — it is outside what we treat as regular work.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you copy an instrument spring from a sample?',
    a: 'Yes. Send an unused spring if you still have one. We measure it and quote within 24 hours.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the minimum order?',
    a: `Usually ${site.terms.moq}. Smaller development runs are charged.`,
  },
];
---

<IndustryLayout
  route="instrumentation"
  title="Instrumentation Spring Manufacturer, Pune"
  description="Light springs for instruments and control gear, wire Ø 0.40–2.50 mm. Made to drawing or sample in Talawade, Pune."
  h1="Instrumentation springs"
  lede="Light, precise springs for instruments and control gear. The same 0.40–2.50 mm wire we use on the rest of the floor."
  context="instrumentation springs"
  faqs={faqs}
  service={{ audience: 'Makers of instruments and control gear' }}
  related={[
    { to: 'extension', label: 'Tension / extension springs', description: 'Returns and floats.' },
    { to: 'torsion', label: 'Torsion springs', description: 'Levers and resets.' },
    {
      to: 'reverseEngineering',
      label: 'Reverse engineering',
      description: 'From a sample when there is no drawing.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2>Light springs, tight pockets</h2>
  <p>
    Instrumentation is one of the industries we serve. The parts are small: a return on a pointer, a
    bias on a switch, a light compression spring in a sensor housing. Wire toward the bottom of our{' '}
    {site.capability.wireRangeLabel} range is common.
  </p>
  <p>
    Level and flow instruments are a typical home for these springs.
    <Todo text="permission to describe a customer anonymously (for example a Pune maker of level and flow instruments)." />
  </p>

  <h2>What to send</h2>
  <p>
    A dimensioned drawing is best. If you only have the old spring, send an unused one — a used
    instrument spring has often taken set, and copying that length will sit short in the assembly.
    Say where it lives (oil, outdoor, a sealed box) so we can pick hard-drawn or stainless.
  </p>
  <p>
    The quote is from the drawing or the sample. You try the development piece in the instrument
    before we run the bulk quantity.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    Wire {site.capability.wireRangeLabel}. Usual minimum {site.terms.moq}. Quote within 24 hours.
    Ex-works Talawade. Across India; no export.
  </p>
</IndustryLayout>
